     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\nHi,\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thanks for your interest in CODEX. For the fractional mode, the segmentation can occur as either large region with neutral copy numbers or small region with non-neutral copy numbers. The first occasion isn’t interesting (whose estimated copy number\r\n is close to 2). If you look at the column named ‘copy_no’ in the output you attached, you can filter out segments with copy number close to 2. We used 1.7 and 2.3 for our cancer genomics sequencing pipeline.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Hope this answers your question. I am cc’ing our mailing list in case other users have similar questions.</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Cheers,</div>\r\n<div>Yuchao</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n<div>On Feb 2, 2016, at 3:51 AM, 韩苗 &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">miao...@3dmedcare.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">Yuchao,<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">Thanks for your excellent work about CODEX.<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">I am worrying about “</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">For the &quot;fraction&quot; mode post segmentation thresholding is necessary to fiter out long CNV events with factional copy numbers close to 2.</span><span style=\"font-family:宋体\">“</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\"><u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">The below is my code and output by setting mode = &quot;fraction&quot;.<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">finalcall &lt;- segment(Y_qc, Yhat, optK = optK, K = K, sampname_qc,ref_qc, chr, lmax = 200, mode = &quot;fraction&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">sample_name  chr   cnv  st_bp       ed_bp      length_kb       st_exon   ed_exon  raw_cov  norm_cov       copy_no  lratio       mBIC       pvalue<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">NA12761       22    dup  21990671       22035729       45.059    25    32    838  704  2.381      12.006    1.025      9.57e-07<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">NA18990       22    dup  22312814       22326373       13.56      60    72    1382       988  2.798      69.785    59.183    3.31e-32<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">NA18990       22    del   21346453       22300470       954.018   1     59    6268       6860       1.827      26.342    81.19       3.92e-13<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">NA19210       22    del   22329961       22599725       269.765   75    76    140  205  1.366      11.612    2.944      1.44e-06<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:CMR10\">Can you tell me how to set “post segmentation thresholding”?<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;background-color:white\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:微软雅黑,sans-serif\">韩苗</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:11.5pt;font-family:微软雅黑,sans-serif\"><u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:left;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\">\r\n<hr size=\"1\" width=\"210\" noshade align=\"left\" style=\"width:157.5pt\">\r\n</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;text-align:justify;font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;line-height:15.75pt;background-color:white\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:宋体;background-color:white\">地址：</span><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span> </span></span><span style=\"font-family:宋体;background-color:white\">上海市闵行区浦江漕河泾高科技园区新骏环路</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family:Arial,